ies; and operates video production companies and studio production facilities. The company was formerly known as Gray Television, Inc. and changed its name to Gray Media, Inc. in July 2002. Gray Media, Inc. was founded in 1891 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Hilton Hatchett Howell Jr. | Executive Chairman & CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $338K ranks in the bottom quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 18%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Gray Media, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $644M market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +18% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $181M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 7.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 100% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5617070357554781},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Communication Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 78% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Gray Media (GTN) Upgraded to Buy: Here's What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036805/gray-media-gtn-upgraded-to-buy-here-s-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3036805","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795795204.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","analyst_action"]},{"title":"GTN Limited Issues Shares Under Employee I